WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.265
Easy Folk Tales. The Elves and the Shoemaker.

00:00:03.265 --> 00:00:06.624
There was once a good shoemaker who had become very poor.

00:00:06.624 --> 00:00:10.627
At last he had only enough leather for one pair of shoes.

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:13.859
He cut out the leather in the evening and went to bed.

00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:17.698
In the morning he found a finished pair of shoes on his table.

00:00:17.698 --> 00:00:19.285
They were beautifully made.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:24.660
A man came into the shop and liked them so much that he paid twice the usual price.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.737
Now the shoemaker could buy leather for two pairs.

00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:29.608
He cut the leather that evening.

00:00:29.608 --> 00:00:32.599
In the morning two pairs of shoes stood on the table.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.413
He sold them and bought leather for four pairs.

00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:37.965
And so it went on, night after night.

00:00:37.965 --> 00:00:40.423
Soon the shoemaker was a rich man.

00:00:40.423 --> 00:00:46.734
One evening before Christmas he said to his wife, "Let us stay awake tonight and see who is helping us."

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.090
They hid behind a curtain and watched.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.572
At midnight two tiny men came in.

00:00:51.572 --> 00:00:53.452
They wore no clothes at all.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:56.199
They sat down at the table and began to work.

00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:01.160
Their little fingers moved so fast that the shoemaker could not believe his eyes.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.019
When all the shoes were finished, they ran away.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:07.049
"Those little men have made us rich," said the wife.

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:08.983
"And they must be so cold.

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:14.663
I will make them shirts, coats and trousers, and you can make them each a tiny pair of shoes."

00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:18.814
On Christmas night they put the presents on the table and hid again.

00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:20.988
At midnight the elves came in.

00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:24.156
When they saw the little clothes, they laughed with joy.

00:01:24.156 --> 00:01:28.933
They put them on and danced around the room, over the chairs and out of the door.

00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:30.310
They never came back.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.454
But the shoemaker and his wife did well for the rest of their lives.
